# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for xournal-qt test runs (how to run them: qt/docs/testing/README.md, "ThreadSanitizer").
#
# Only libraries that are not built with -fsanitize=thread and code that is outside the fork's reach go here, each with
# its reason. A race in qt/ code is fixed, not suppressed; one too big to fix now is listed in TODO.md.
#
# TSan sees what instrumented code does and what goes through the interceptors (pthread, malloc, memcpy, ...). The
# libraries below come prebuilt (conda-forge, the system): what they synchronise with atomics or locks of their own is
# invisible, so it shows up as races, and so does every hand-off through them.

# --- Qt (prebuilt, not instrumented) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A job handed to a QThreadPool (ImageWorkers, BackgroundJobs, the library index, the save and merge workers, the PDF
# cache eviction) is queued under Qt's own mutex (futex based, invisible): TSan sees no order between the thread that
# started the job and the job. Every pool job's first touch of what it was given is reported. With this, pool jobs are
# not checked against the threads that start them; that needs a Qt built with -sanitize thread.
race:QThreadPoolThread::run
race:QThreadPoolPrivate::enqueueTask
race:QRunnable::QGenericRunnable
# The same for calls queued to another thread (QMetaObject::invokeMethod with Qt::QueuedConnection, queued signals,
# upstream's Util::execInUiThread through AppContext::installQtUiThreadDispatcher): posted under Qt's event queue lock.
race:QCoreApplicationPrivate::sendPostedEvents
race:QMetaCallEvent
race:QMetaObject::invokeMethodImpl
race:installQtUiThreadDispatcher
# A QThread's start hands its object to the new thread (Qt's own thread data, its start mutex).
race:QThread::start
# Implicitly shared Qt data (QString, QByteArray, QList, QImage) handed between threads: its reference count and
# its memory are managed inside Qt (QArrayData::allocate/reallocate, QWaitCondition of a pool that goes).
race:QArrayData::allocate
race:QArrayData::reallocateUnaligned
race:QWaitCondition::~QWaitCondition
# QImage's conversions and smooth scaling split the work onto Qt's internal pool (qt_qimageScale*, convert_generic).
race:convert_generic
race:multithread_pixels_function
race:handleSpans

# --- C libraries (prebuilt, not instrumented) ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cairo's pattern and clip freelists and its FreeType font map use cairo's own atomics; the pages are drawn on several
# render threads at once, each with cairo objects of its own (same pattern as upstream Xournal++).
race:libcairo.so.2
# glibc's time zone state (localtime_r, mktime, also through Qt's qMkTime) is guarded by a lock internal to glibc.
race:tzset_internal
# Poppler draws one page of an instance at a time under its own mutex and shares its global caches the same way.
race:libpoppler.so
race:libpoppler-glib.so
# Text layout on several render threads: fontconfig, Pango and HarfBuzz synchronise internally.
called_from_lib:libfontconfig.so.1
called_from_lib:libpangoft2-1.0.so.0
called_from_lib:libpango-1.0.so.0
called_from_lib:libharfbuzz.so.0
race:libglib-2.0.so.0
race:libfontconfig.so.1
race:libpangoft2-1.0.so.0
# Lock bookkeeping inside the same uninstrumented libraries (GRWLock / GType class locks used by pango).
mutex:libglib-2.0.so.0
mutex:libgobject-2.0.so.0
deadlock:libglib-2.0.so.0
deadlock:libgobject-2.0.so.0

# --- Upstream Xournal++ code (outside qt/, not changed by the fork) -------------------------------------------------
# An element computes its size the first time it is asked (Element::getBoundingBox -> calcSize, a `mutable` cache).
# The render threads ask under the shared document lock, so two of them, or a render and the UI thread copying the
# page for a save (Text::clone), may compute it at once. They write the same values; the fork's seam in
# Element::getBoundingBox sets the flag only after the size, so no thread uses half a size. A data race all the same:
# TODO.md ("Canvas: ... the lazy element size").
race:Element::getBoundingBox
race:calcSize
# Upstream's QPdfExport::overlayAndSave gives QPDFWriter a temporary file name (u8string().data()); qpdf keeps the
# pointer and reads it when it makes the file's /ID: a read after free inside qpdf (the fork's own writers keep the
# name alive). Reported for upstream in TODO.md.
race:QPdfExport::overlayAndSave
race:HybridPdfExport::createPdf
